Seam: RegisterLocalState in chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc, among the
      calls that ask each subsystem to register the settings it owns, and the
      dep that lets that file see them.
Why: how updates are allowed to arrive is one setting for the installation
     rather than one per profile -- there is one application on disk and
     every profile runs from it -- and local state is where Chromium keeps
     settings of that kind. No seam existed here yet, because this is the
     first setting Arcium owns that is not part of its own model file.
Delegates to: arcium::RegisterUpdatePrefs
